A||||8||BOILERMAKER||Windshield Wipers - Cycle on Start||||
Z||000000||BOILERMAKER||08-06-99||05:13 PM||||I have an 87 SE column in an 86 GT and whenever I start up the car after sitting for awhile, the windshield wipers cycle.  It seems as if there is a capacitance somewhere and it worked fine in the 87 SE.  I have the column with the thumb buttons.  I didn't like the original GT column and switched.<p>Is there a capacitor somewhere that I have to lose?  The wiper delay works find along with the other functions of the stock, but this cycle thing on startup is annoying.<p>Thanks
Z||000001||Cooter||08-06-99||07:59 PM||||My Suburban does the same thing, I have just learned to live with it because the switch and delay timer is fine. The only other thing it might be is the wiper motor itself. If the "park" contacts in the motor are going out, I guess they could cause this problem. If you have another wiper motor, just swap them and see if the problem goes away.
Z||000002||Dave85||08-06-99||09:19 PM||||I have the same problem. Mine also comes on once in a while when turning on the turn signal. I figured I just have a short in the switch.? 
Z||000003||rcn491||08-06-99||11:07 PM||||Mine ran all the time unless I  pulled the fuse. After pulling the sterring wheel etc., I found that the problem was in the small circuit board on the wiper motor. Your problem could be there.
Z||000004||burdell1||08-07-99||07:46 AM||||rcn491,<p>What did you do to fix yours? Mine has done the same thing, and then I replaced the circuit board and it does it again eventually. I figure something isn't grounded properly, but I haven't found out what yet.
Z||000005||kel||08-07-99||02:45 PM||||Hmmm... this must be one of those "common" problems.  Mine also takes one swipe sometimes when I use the turn signal and sometimes when I drive over railroad tracks! 
Z||000006||Bruce||08-07-99||06:35 PM||||When I first bought mine, it did the same thing. While I was getting the recall done, I had the blinker/wiper switch mechanism on the steering column replaced. That ended the problem.
Z||000007||BOILERMAKER||09-10-1999||05:47 PM||||I haven't found the answer for it yet, but I have found some new developments.  Sometimes it stops midway.  When I hit the mist switch early in the morning (and sometimes during the day) the wipers take sometimes 7 swipes before they stop.<P>Also, my windshield washers don't work now.  I am thinking I have some electric gremlins.||||reg||
Z||000008||BOILERMAKER||09-13-1999||09:01 AM||||I switched out the windshield wiper module this weekend and the darn thing works great now.  Looks like I found my gremlins.||||reg||11
